      "external_credits": 22,
      "external_note": "CSU GE-Breadth (new structure effective Fall 2025) totals 43 units across Area 1 (English Communication & Critical Thinking, 9), Area 2 (Mathematics/Quantitative Reasoning, 3), Area 3 (Arts & Humanities, 6), Area 4 (Social Sciences, 6), Area 5 (Physical & Biological Sciences, 7), Area 6 (Ethnic Studies, 3), plus 9 upper-division GE units. Per the program page, 21 of the 43 GE units are met by required major courses (ENGL 2030 -> Area 1A; MATH 2110 -> Area 2; PHYS 2100 -> Area 5A; CS 3801 plus the upper-division GE block are met in major). The remaining 22 GE units are taken outside the major and modeled here as an external wildcard pool. Also includes the 6-unit American Institutions (US History + US/State Constitution & Government), two diversity (d) courses (one meeting (re)/race & ethnicity), a Civic Learning/Community Engagement course, and Writing-Intensive courses, which CSU GE-Breadth double-counts within the 43 units.",
