  "conversion_warnings": [
    "catalog_year 2025-2026 confirmed from the live program page (Modern Campus catoid=75).",
    "degree_type BS confirmed per catalog (Bachelor of Science in Computer Science).",
    "cip_code 11.0701 (Computer Science) inferred from program name; not stated in catalog.",
    "Major structure per the live program page: Lower Division Core 43 units (12 courses), Upper Division Core 32 units (11 courses), Upper Division Electives 18 units = 93 major units total, matching the catalog's stated 'Major Units: 93'.",
    "Upper Division Electives modeled as a type:select pool over all 19 catalog options (18 CS 4xxx courses + EE 3445), credits:18, exclude_used:true. CS 4540 (Topics) is catalog variable 1-3 units, repeatable to 20 units; modeled at 3.0 units for pool purposes.",
    "Corrected from skeletal source: MATH 2120 listed MATH 2110 as a COREQUISITE in the skeleton, but the live catalog states 'Prerequisite: C or higher in MATH 2110' -> remodeled as a prerequisite. CS 4540 credit_hours corrected 1.0 -> 3.0 (catalog lists 3 units, variable 1-3) and marked repeatable.",
    "Corrected from skeletal source: the skeleton split CS courses into 'cs_course_core' (all 22 incl. ENGL/MATH/PHYS) and a single 'picklist_upper-division-electives' (count:18, miscategorized as category:elective). Rebuilt into Lower Division Core (43u), Upper Division Core (32u, category:major), and Upper Division Electives (18u, category:major); the elective block now uses credits:18 rather than count:18 (the catalog states '18 units', and CS 4540 can be 1-3 units so a count is inaccurate).",
    "Prerequisites/corequisites carried from the skeletal source (same source catalog) and spot-verified against the live course catalog: CS 3337 corequisite ENGL 2030 retained; CS 4963 corequisite CS 4962 retained; CS 4961 requires the full upper-division core chain. CS 4540 (Topics) has no fixed prerequisite (consent/varies) and is left without a prereq to avoid a dangling/invalid reference.",
    "General Education modeled as ONE external wildcard select pool ('*:*', external_requirement:true). CSU GE-Breadth (new structure, Fall 2025) is 43 units; the program page states 21 of those 43 units are met by required major courses (ENGL 2030 -> Area 1A Written Communication; MATH 2110 -> Area 2 Quantitative Reasoning; PHYS 2100 -> Area 5A Physical Science; CS 3801 + the 9 upper-division GE units 'met in major'). Only the 22 GE units taken OUTSIDE the major are counted in requirements to avoid double-counting major credits.",
    "American Institutions (6u: US History + US/State Constitution & Government), the two diversity (d) courses (one (re)/race-and-ethnicity), Civic Learning/Community Engagement, and the Writing-Intensive requirement are folded into the 22-unit external GE pool because CSU GE-Breadth double-counts them within the 43 GE units.",
    "Credit reconciliation: Lower Division Core 43 + Upper Division Core 32 + Upper Division Electives 18 + GE-outside-major 22 + Free Electives 5 = 120 = total_credits. Major = 93 (matches catalog). GE = 43 (21 met by major, 22 external). A minimum of 40 units overall must be upper division (not separately modeled).",
    "Free Electives set to 5 units to close the gap to the 120-unit minimum after major (93) and GE-outside-major (22)."
  ]
